# EmitterApp conventions

## Structure and scope

- Preserve the current package layout; do not move files unless the user asks.
- Keep changes minimal: only what the task requires; no drive-by refactors or unrelated edits.

## Architecture

- Follow existing patterns: Compose + ViewModel for UI; `domain` interfaces and models; `data` for repository implementations; use cases where the feature already uses them.
- Prefer extending or modifying existing functions over duplicating logic or adding parallel helpers.
- Before proposing edits, read related files in the same package for naming, types, and style.

## Kotlin and Compose

- Match surrounding import style, abstraction level, and documentation density.
- Comments: concise, English only; do not remove existing comments; avoid obvious docstrings.

## Strings and localization

- User-visible text belongs in resources, not hardcoded in Kotlin.
- Add or update keys in [app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml](app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml) and [app/src/main/res/values-es/strings.xml](app/src/main/res/values-es/strings.xml) together with matching keys.

## When the task is unclear

- If there is no concrete feature, bug, or refactor target, ask the user to specify the desired outcome before large changes.
